  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Here&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;represents&nbsp;a circle with center <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">n</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;represents&nbsp;a circle with center&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&#8745;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></math>, both circles do not intersect each other.</p><p>When&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#62;</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></math><br />then possible values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>When&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#60;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p>then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;has infinite solutions for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi></math></p><p>Hence, there are total four values possible.</p></blockquote><p>&nbsp;</p>"
